('34', 'Python’s Hidden Number Feature | Python Tutorial', 'In this Python tutorial, you\'ll learn how underscore separators work in numbers like 1_000_000. Python ignores the underscores when running the code, but they make large numbers much easier to read. You\'ll also see why other characters like commas or dashes do not work inside Python numbers. #python #pythontutorial #pythontricks #learnpython #pythonbeginners #coding #programming #python3 #cleancode #developer #softwaredevelopment #pythonexamples #codetutorial #100DaysOfCode #computerscience #pythoncoding #pythonfeature #beginnerpython', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mJEIsjSMPDk', '40', '2025-10-31'),
('56', 'R programming tutorial | Calculating quantiles in R', 'Given a fraction f, you want to know the corresponding quantile of your data. That is, you seek the observation x such that the fraction of observations below x is f. quantile(vec, f) where vec is a vector or a variable of a data frame in R. #rstudio #rprogramming #quantile #rdatacode', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YmIxsxdphI0', '273', '2026-01-07'),
('50', '10 Key Breakthrough Technologies of 2025', 'Portuguese and Spanish language translations for SXSW 2025 Keynotes and Featured Sessions presented by Itaú Each year, MIT Technology Review reporters and editors assemble a list of the top breakthrough technologies that will change the world. This list is one of our most popular packages of the year. Niall Firth will share the publication’s list of ten breakthrough technologies with the SXSW audience, explaining each one and how it will impact the way we live and work. About SXSW: SXSW dedicates itself to helping creative people achieve their goals. Founded in 1987 in Austin, Texas, SXSW is best known for its conference and festivals that celebrate the convergence of the interactive, film, and music industries. An essential destination for global professionals, SXSW features sessions, showcases, screenings, exhibitions, professional development and a variety of networking opportunities. For more information, please visit sxsw.com. Subscribe: http://www.youtube.com/user/sxsw?sub_...', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=srQwyArPnP8', '3234', '2026-03-02'),
